Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:10:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build/InterpreterStartup: the interpreter startup
 (Turing.exists_interpreterStartup), harvested from the core's eleven phases;
 NDCodeSimulator's core re-pointed to it

The startup is generalized over the installed machine family, the installer (the shape of
FinTM.exists_installCallTM's contract) and a number of passive tapes. The core cites it at
four passive tapes (the stream, the loop's two banks and its capture), keeping only its hosted
loop; its statement is unchanged. NDCodeSimulator: 2,384 -> 1,412 lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
